cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TaxRiskScan in research, please cite it as below, and cite the data sources listed in DATA_SOURCES.md."
title: "TaxRiskScan: profit-shifting and Pillar Two screening for country-by-country reporting data"
abstract: >-
  Open-source tool that screens Country-by-Country Reporting (CbCR) data for low taxation,
  profit shifting and Pillar Two exposure. It combines a rule engine linked to EU and OECD
  legal sources, a logistic-regression classifier trained on public CbCRs (EU Tax Observatory)
  and k-means anomaly detection, with Transitional CbCR Safe Harbour tests and a
  dataset-level research mode.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Mahdavi Shirkharkolaei"
    given-names: "Alireza"
version: 3.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-15
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/AlirezaMahdavishirkharkolaei/Tax_Risk_AI"
keywords:
  - international taxation
  - profit shifting
  - country-by-country reporting
  - Pillar Two
  - global minimum tax
  - tax havens
  - legal technology
  - machine learning
references:
